  "reason": "DEF g12 scythe strike: the capture left the scythe hanging at the side in the left hand while only the free arm waved. AttackFront now levels the scythe two-handed at chest height pointing back (f1), swings it up and back over the shoulder with the torso leaning back (f2-f3), sweeps it forward level at the waist with a forward lean (f4), and follows through down-front, holding the diagonal to the end (f5-f7). LeftHand is aimed by the shaft's local axis; both arms are re-aimed so the hands stay together on the shaft. stretchRelax evens the shoulder edges of the overhead swing.",
